## 4. Tenant data and AI credentials

You must keep tenant-specific data within systems and accounts controlled by
you or your organization, except for data sent to your chosen AI provider as
needed to process your queries. That exception may include selected directory
records and query results, not just query text. It does not authorize unrelated
external sharing of tenant data. You are responsible for authorizing that
processing and configuring the deployment accordingly.

You must use your own authorized AI provider credentials, keep them private,
and not share or redistribute provider keys to third parties. Secure use of
those credentials within your own authorized deployment is permitted.

